.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-payments-update - Change a payment's description, internal note or reference


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 payments update  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Change the off-chain fields of a payment, in any status, closed ones included.
They live only on the gateway — in nothing signed or hashed on-chain — so this
moves no money, needs no signing key and sends no webhook.

.PP
--description / --clear   either party; at most 255 characters. --clear
                            removes it (not both).
  --note                    the PAYEE's internal note, at most 2000 characters;
                            never shown to the payer.
  --reference               the payment's identifier in your own system (e.g.
                            an order number there), at most 128 characters.
  --reference-origin        which system that is: a lowercase slug, e.g.
                            commercelayer.

.PP
The last three are the payee's: the payer gets 403 not_the_payee. Pass one
as "" to clear it; clearing the reference clears its origin too. Only the
flags given are sent, and at least one is required.

.PP
Requires login — run 'rail0 auth login -p 0xKey…' first.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--clear\fP[=false]
	Remove the description

.PP
\fB-d\fP, \fB--description\fP=""
	New description (max 255 characters)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for update

.PP
\fB--note\fP=""
	The payee's internal note, never shown to the payer ("" clears it)

.PP
\fB--reference\fP=""
	The payment's identifier in your own system ("" clears it and its origin)

.PP
\fB--reference-origin\fP=""
	Which system the reference comes from: a lowercase slug, e.g. commercelayer


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 payments update 0xabc123… -d "spring collection"
  rail0 payments update 0xabc123… --clear
  rail0 payments update 0xabc123… --note "refund agreed by email"
  rail0 payments update 0xabc123… --reference ORD-1042 --reference-origin commercelayer
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-payments(1)\fP
